        "thread_id": "TH3",
        "thread_goal": "Align on daily maintenance routine, responsibilities, and tracking approach.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M40",
            "speaker_id": 315682,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Team, let's talk about keeping the demo zone in top shape. I've created a draft for the daily maintenance checklist (A3) as part of T5. It covers cleaning, cable checks, and making sure everything is powered on. Feedback welcome.",
            "mentions": [
              106421,
              173570,
              390795
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3",
              "T5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M41",
            "speaker_id": 106421,
            "reply_to": "M40",
            "text": "The checklist in A3 looks comprehensive. I timed myself doing a quick run-through of the steps, and it takes about 10 minutes, which is perfectly reasonable for a daily task.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thumbsup",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M42",
            "speaker_id": 390795,
            "reply_to": "M40",
            "text": "Who has to do this? Is it the first person in the department each day?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M43",
            "speaker_id": 315682,
            "reply_to": "M42",
            "text": "Good question. To ensure it's always done, I propose the first person on the morning shift is responsible for the initial check, and the first person on the afternoon shift does a quick tidy-up. We can have a sign-off sheet next to the checklist. Does that sound fair?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M44",
            "speaker_id": 106421,
            "reply_to": "M43",
            "text": "That works. It spreads the responsibility and ensures it's checked twice a day. I'm happy with that.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M45",
            "speaker_id": 173570,
            "reply_to": "M43",
            "text": "ok",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M46",
            "speaker_id": 315682,
            "reply_to": "M44",
            "text": "Perfect, let's formalize that. The checklist is approved, and ownership is with the first person on the morning and afternoon shifts. That's D5.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M47",
            "speaker_id": 315682,
            "reply_to": "M46",
            "text": "Related to this is T10, tracking our success. I've set up a simple sales tracking sheet in A6. It has columns for date, product, bundles sold, and the seller's name. The goal is to see how the demo zone impacts sales.",
            "mentions": [
              106421,
              173570,
              390795
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T10",
              "A6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M48",
            "speaker_id": 106421,
            "reply_to": "M47",
            "text": "The sheet A6 is straightforward. When should we fill it out? After each sale, or at the end of the day?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M49",
            "speaker_id": 315682,
            "reply_to": "M48",
            "text": "I think filling it out right after the sale is best, so we don't forget the details. It should only take 30 seconds. We can keep a tablet or a printed copy at the main counter for easy access.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M50",
            "speaker_id": 173570,
            "reply_to": "M49",
            "text": "a printed copy is easier i think",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M51",
            "speaker_id": 315682,
            "reply_to": "M50",
            "text": "We can do both. A printed copy for quick notes, and someone can digitize it at the end of the day. Let's agree that the seller who makes the sale is responsible for logging it immediately. That's our process. Agreed?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M52",
            "speaker_id": 106421,
            "reply_to": "M51",
            "text": "Yes, that works. Immediate logging is the most accurate way.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M53",
            "speaker_id": 390795,
            "reply_to": "M51",
            "text": "agreed",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M54",
            "speaker_id": 315682,
            "reply_to": "M53",
            "text": "Excellent. Decision D6 is made: sales will be tracked by the seller immediately after the transaction. I'll finalize A3 and A6 and share them in the main project folder.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3",
              "A6"
            ],
